There are multiple things you should pay attention to when buying an electric scooter and here we will cover all of them.
The first thing you should pay attention to is…
The first factor to keep in mind is the motor size and the overall speed of the scooter. You should think about what you are going to be doing on your scooter to help make this consideration.
These are all factors that affect what type of motor you need or what type of motor you might want. Scooters with larger motors are going to cost more and they are going to be heavier so they may not be great for commuting.
Tires can affect how smooth your ride is, how much power is exerted by your scooter, and how efficient your scooter is. With scooters that are going to be driven or ridden on smooth terrain, air-filled tires are not as important.
If you are going to be driving off-road you do need tires that are air-filled to help make the ride smoother and more enjoyable overall in terms of comfort and stability of the ride and drive. This can also relate to suspension.
You should also be keeping the battery size and the battery range in mind. Are you going to be commuting a longer distance, shorter distances, staying in a small area, are you going to be driving off-road?
Maxing out the weight capacity on your scooter is going to make it go slower, it is going to make the battery run down faster and it can also cause unneeded wear and tear on your scooter.
