Here are some of the possible causes and the solutions explained step by step so that you can solve the cases in which your mobile does not recognize SIM card:
Although modern mobiles include slots in which it can only fit one way, it is possible that some models allow it to be inserted one way or another. To solve this problem:
If it was incorrectly placed, once it is correctly you can check that everything works normally.
Take out the card tray. Make sure that they have not come out of the socket and therefore cannot be inserted because they are colliding.
Take the SIM card out of its slot.
You can blow or wipe the surface if you see dirt. Do it with a dry cloth, never with something damp.
This happens when the card is too old and has passed from one mobile to another, deteriorating the gold contacts or due to a crack. If you see visual damage, the solution is to ask your technology provider to clone the card or ask for a new one.
This usually happens in old mobile devices, or in which the card has been removed and inserted very frequently. To check if this is the case, follow these steps:
Take out the SIM card inside.
Test if it detects that other card. If not, it will indicate that there is physical damage to the mobile.
Contact your telephone service provider and certify that the SIM card has been activated. If it was an old card, this step will not be necessary.
In the search engine type "SIM" and you will get several related options.
And in data / call SIM, which is active. If it isn't, press the enable switch.
