Temperature control: For extrusion production, extrusion temperature is the most basic and critical process factor. Extrusion temperature has great influence on product quality, production efficiency, die life and energy consumption.
Extrusion speed: The extrusion speed must be carefully controlled during the extrusion process. The extrusion speed has important influence on the thermal effect of deformation, deformation uniformity, recrystallization and solid solution process, mechanical properties and surface quality of products.
Machine quenching: The 6063-T5 quenching is to preserve the Mg2Si solid dissolved in the matrix metal at high temperature after the mold hole is quickly cooled to room temperature. The cooling rate is usually proportional to the content of the hardening phase.
