As laptops and tablets have gotten thinner and lighter, some features have been eliminated.The first thing to disappear is usually multiple USB ports.If you’re lucky, you can buy a laptop with more than two ports today.But gadgets like Apple’s MacBook have only one USB port.If you already have a wired keyboard or mouse plugged in, you’ll have to make another plan to access the external hard drive.
When looking at the specifications for a USB 3.0 hub, you’ll notice that some ports are designated differently than others.That’s because ports usually come in two varieties: data and charging.
Meanwhile, the charging port is exactly what it sounds like.While it can’t transfer data, it’s used to quickly charge any connected device.In this case, gadgets such as mobile phones, power banks or wireless keyboards can be charged.
Remember, the charging port needs to draw power from a power source.If the hub is not connected to a wall outlet’s power adapter, it will use the laptop’s power to charge the device.This will drain the laptop’s battery faster.
The most important aspect that most people will look for is the number of USB ports on the hub.Simply put, the more ports you have available, the more gadgets you can connect or charge.Anything from phones and tablets to keyboards and mice can go through the hub.
If you need to connect a lot of gadgets, this hub has 7 USB 3.0 ports that can transfer data at 5 Gb per second.It also features three PowerIQ charging ports, each with an output of 2.1 amps, allowing you to charge your device while connected to a laptop or computer.Sold by Amazon
The hub has seven USB 3.0 data ports and two fast-charging USB ports.The chip inside automatically recognizes the connected device to provide the fastest charging speed.It has built-in protection against overcharging, overheating, and power surges.Sold by Amazon
Featuring four USB 3.0 ports, this data hub is a slim, compact solution to connectivity issues.While it can’t charge any connected device, it can transfer data at 5 gigabits per second.The hub is compatible with Windows and Apple devices.Sold by Amazon
