IP is Ingress Protection,which is an international numeric classification to indicate the degrees of protection provided by enclosures for electrical equipment against environmental conditions. It provides a means of specifying the capacity of an enclosue to protect its contents from external solids and liquids in accordance with IEC 60598-1:2003.
0 : No protection, no special protection.
2 : Objects larger than 12 mm are prevented from entering. Preventing the finger from touching the inside of the light.
4 : To prevent intrusion of objects exceeding 1.0 mm.
2: Protection against water droplets deflected up to 15° from vertical
6: Protection against direct high pressure jets.
